You are given three arrays of length n that describe the properties of n coupons: code, businessLine, and isActive. The ith coupon has:

code[i]: a string representing the coupon identifier.
businessLine[i]: a string denoting the business category of the coupon.
isActive[i]: a boolean indicating whether the coupon is currently active.
A coupon is considered valid if all of the following conditions hold:

code[i] is non-empty and consists only of alphanumeric characters (a-z, A-Z, 0-9) and underscores (_).
businessLine[i] is one of the following four categories: "electronics", "grocery", "pharmacy", "restaurant".
isActive[i] is true.
Return an array of the codes of all valid coupons, sorted first by their businessLine in the order: "electronics", "grocery", "pharmacy", "restaurant", and then by code in lexicographical (ascending) order within each category.
 
SOLUTION

from typing import List
class Solution:
    def validateCoupons(self, code: List[str], businessLine: List[str], isActive: List[bool]) -> List[str]:
        order = ["electronics", "grocery", "pharmacy", "restaurant"]
        order_index = {b: i for i, b in enumerate(order)}
        res = []

        for i in range(len(code)):
            if not isActive[i]:
                continue
            if businessLine[i] not in order_index:
                continue
            if not code[i] or not all(c.isalnum() or c == "_" for c in code[i]):
                continue
            res.append((order_index[businessLine[i]], code[i]))

        res.sort()
        return [c for _, c in res]
